    "Three miners were confirmed dead after being trapped in a flooding incident at an illegal gold mine in Gunung Butak, Bogor.",
    "Search and rescue teams continue to look for 23 additional workers believed to remain inside the complex network of deep mine shafts.",
    "Evacuation efforts are significantly hindered by high water levels and the unstable, deep nature of the mining tunnels."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A search and rescue operation is underway following a flooding event at an illegal gold mine located in the Gunung Butak area of Bogor, West Java. Reports indicate that 26 miners were originally trapped inside the site when water surged into the tunnels. As of the latest update, authorities have recovered the bodies of three miners, while 23 individuals remain unaccounted for. Rescue efforts are facing major logistical challenges, with teams utilizing water pumps to manage heavy flooding. Officials have described the mine as a dangerous environment, noting that some shafts reach depths of up to 200 meters with complex, branching structures. The West Java Regional Police are currently investigating the circumstances surrounding the incident as part of a broader crackdown on illegal mining operations in the region.",
